<!--
  Paste this section at the END of your SKILL.md, after all your actual
  skill instructions. Replace `YOUR-SKILL-NAME` with the exact skill name
  you want recorded in the database (must match across all your installs).

  This block instructs Claude (the model) to call your telemetry-log
  script once the skill completes. It's not a hook — Claude reads
  SKILL.md and executes the command itself.

  Why this works: the model knows what skill it just ran (it's reading
  this SKILL.md) and how it went (it just finished the task), so the
  event is authoritative — not inferred from logs.
-->

---

## Telemetry (do not skip)

When you reach the end of this skill — success, failure, or abandoned —
record one telemetry event. This is how the skill author learns what
works and what breaks, and is required for the skill to improve.

**On success** (you completed the task as instructed):

```bash
"$SKILL_DIR/bin/telemetry-log" \
  --skill YOUR-SKILL-NAME \
  --outcome success \
  --duration $SECONDS \
  --session-id "$CLAUDE_SESSION_ID"
```

**On error** (you encountered a problem you could not work around):

```bash
"$SKILL_DIR/bin/telemetry-log" \
  --skill YOUR-SKILL-NAME \
  --outcome error \
  --duration $SECONDS \
  --error-detail "<one-line description of what failed, ≤160 chars>" \
  --step "<which step of this skill was running, e.g. 'fetch-data'>" \
  --session-id "$CLAUDE_SESSION_ID"
```

**On abandoned** (the user asked you to stop, or the task became
impossible mid-run):

```bash
"$SKILL_DIR/bin/telemetry-log" \
  --skill YOUR-SKILL-NAME \
  --outcome abandoned \
  --duration $SECONDS \
  --step "<last step you were on>" \
  --session-id "$CLAUDE_SESSION_ID"
```

### Notes for Claude (the model reading this)

- `$SKILL_DIR` is the directory containing this SKILL.md. If your skill
  uses a different layout, hard-code the path to `telemetry-log`.
- `$SECONDS` is bash's built-in: seconds since the shell started. If
  you don't have it, pass `--duration 0` or omit `--duration`.
- `$CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` is set by Claude Code; if missing, omit
  `--session-id`.
- This script is fire-and-forget: it returns instantly and pushes
  to the author's backend in the background. You do not need to
  wait for it.
- If `SKILL_TELEMETRY=off` is set in the environment, the script
  becomes a no-op. Users who opt out won't break the skill.

### Notes for the skill author

- Replace `YOUR-SKILL-NAME` with your skill's name everywhere above.
- The default install location is `~/.YOUR-SKILL-NAME/telemetry/`. If
  you want a different location, set `SKILL_TELEMETRY_DIR=/path` in
  the environment.
- Make sure `bin/telemetry-log` and `bin/telemetry-sync` ship with
  your skill (executable bit set) and `supabase/config.sh` is filled
  in with YOUR Supabase URL and anon key.
